{"info":{"author":null,"author_email":"Mathieu Fenniak <biziqe@mathieu.fenniak.net>","bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":["Development Status :: 5 - Production/Stable","Intended Audience :: Developers","Operating System :: OS Independent","Programming Language :: Python :: 3","Programming Language :: Python :: 3 :: Only","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.13","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.14","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.9","Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules","Typing :: Typed"],"description":"[![PyPI version](https://badge.fury.io/py/pypdf.svg)](https://badge.fury.io/py/pypdf)\n[![Python Support](https://img.shields.io/pypi/pyversions/pypdf.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/pypdf/)\n[![](https://img.shields.io/badge/-documentation-green)](https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/)\n[![GitHub last commit](https://img.shields.io/github/last-commit/py-pdf/pypdf)](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf)\n[![codecov](https://codecov.io/gh/py-pdf/pypdf/branch/main/graph/badge.svg?token=id42cGNZ5Z)](https://codecov.io/gh/py-pdf/pypdf)\n\n# pypdf\n\npypdf is a free and open-source pure-python PDF library capable of splitting,\n[merging](https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user/merging-pdfs.html),\n[cropping, and transforming](https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user/cropping-and-transforming.html)\nthe pages of PDF files. It can also add\ncustom data, viewing options, and\n[passwords](https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user/encryption-decryption.html)\nto PDF files. pypdf can\n[retrieve text](https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user/extract-text.html)\nand\n[metadata](https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user/metadata.html)\nfrom PDFs as well.\n\nSee [pdfly](https://github.com/py-pdf/pdfly) for a CLI application that uses pypdf to interact with PDFs.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall pypdf using pip:\n\n```\npip install pypdf\n```\n\nFor using pypdf with AES encryption or decryption, install extra dependencies:\n\n```\npip install pypdf[crypto]\n```\n\n> **NOTE**: `pypdf` 3.1.0 and above include significant improvements compared to\n> previous versions. Please refer to [the migration\n> guide](https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user/migration-1-to-2.html) for\n> more information.\n\n## Usage\n\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n\nreader = PdfReader(\"example.pdf\")\nnumber_of_pages = len(reader.pages)\npage = reader.pages[0]\ntext = page.extract_text()\n```\n\npypdf can do a lot more, e.g. splitting, merging, reading and creating annotations, decrypting and encrypting. Check out the\n[documentation](https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) for additional usage\nexamples!\n\nFor questions and answers, visit\n[StackOverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/pypdf)\n(tagged with [pypdf](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/pypdf)).\n\n## Contributions\n\nMaintaining pypdf is a collaborative effort. You can support the project by\nwriting documentation, helping to narrow down issues, and submitting code.\nSee the [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) file for more information.\n\n### Q&A\n\nThe experience pypdf users have covers the whole range from beginner to expert. You can contribute to the pypdf community by answering questions\non [StackOverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/pypdf),\nhelping in [discussions](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/discussions),\nand asking users who report issues for [MCVE](https://stackoverflow.com/help/minimal-reproducible-example)'s (Code + example PDF!).\n\n\n### Issues\n\nA good bug ticket includes a MCVE - a minimal complete verifiable example.\nFor pypdf, this means that you must upload a PDF that causes the bug to occur\nas well as the code you're executing with all of the output. Use\n`print(pypdf.__version__)` to tell us which version you're using.\n\n### Code\n\nAll code contributions are welcome, but smaller ones have a better chance to\nget included in a timely manner. Adding unit tests for new features or test\ncases for bugs you've fixed help us to ensure that the Pull Request (PR) is fine.\n\npypdf includes a test suite which can be executed with `pytest`:\n\n```bash\n$ pytest\n===================== test session starts =====================\nplatform linux -- Python 3.6.15, pytest-7.0.1, pluggy-1.0.0\nrootdir: /home/moose/GitHub/Martin/pypdf\nplugins: cov-3.0.0\ncollected 233 items\n\ntests/test_basic_features.py ..                         [  0%]\ntests/test_constants.py .                               [  1%]\ntests/test_filters.py .................x.....           [ 11%]\ntests/test_generic.py ................................. [ 25%]\n.............                                           [ 30%]\ntests/test_javascript.py ..                             [ 31%]\ntests/test_merger.py .                                  [ 32%]\ntests/test_page.py .........................            [ 42%]\ntests/test_pagerange.py ................                [ 49%]\ntests/test_papersizes.py ..................             [ 57%]\ntests/test_reader.py .................................. [ 72%]\n...............                                         [ 78%]\ntests/test_utils.py ....................                [ 87%]\ntests/test_workflows.py ..........                      [ 91%]\ntests/test_writer.py .................                  [ 98%]\ntests/test_xmp.py ...                                   [100%]\n\n========== 232 passed, 1 xfailed, 1 warning in 4.52s ==========\n```\n\n","description_content_type":"text/markdown","docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":null,"home_page":null,"keywords":null,"license":null,"license_expression":"BSD-3-Clause","license_files":["LICENSE"],"maintainer":"stefan6419846","maintainer_email":"Martin Thoma <info@martin-thoma.de>","name":"pypdf","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/pypdf/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/pypdf/","project_urls":{"Bug Reports":"https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/issues","Changelog":"https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/latest/meta/CHANGELOG.html","Documentation":"https://pypdf.readthedocs.io/en/latest/","Source":"https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf"},"provides_extra":["crypto","cryptodome","dev","docs","full","image"],"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/pypdf/6.7.0/","requires_dist":["typing_extensions>=4.0; python_version < \"3.11\"","cryptography; extra == \"crypto\"","PyCryptodome; extra == \"cryptodome\"","flit; extra == \"dev\"","pip-tools; extra == \"dev\"","pre-commit; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-cov; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-socket; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-timeout; extra == \"dev\"","pytest-xdist; extra == \"dev\"","wheel; extra == \"dev\"","myst_parser; extra == \"docs\"","sphinx; extra == \"docs\"","sphinx_rtd_theme; extra == \"docs\"","cryptography; extra == \"full\"","Pillow>=8.0.0; extra == \"full\"","Pillow>=8.0.0; extra == \"image\""],"requires_python":">=3.9","summary":"A pure-python PDF library capable of splitting, merging, cropping, and transforming PDF files","version":"6.7.0","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},"last_serial":41123876,"ownership":{"organization":null,"roles":[{"role":"Owner","user":"Martin.Thoma"},{"role":"Owner","user":"mfenniak"},{"role":"Owner","user":"stefan6419846"}]},"urls":[{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"6c526e96d8753d9392aa78561d86bc40daf3e5b8a42d326477777756728ca7e4"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"edf1c92e75a0eb18bb10845e792054ded113010de958b6d4998e201c029417bb","md5":"981f4e967b9c16f887064c37976f66dd","sha256":"62e85036d50839cbdf45b8067c2c1a1b925517514d7cba4cbe8755a6c2829bc9"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"pypdf-6.7.0-py3-none-any.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"981f4e967b9c16f887064c37976f66dd","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"py3","requires_python":">=3.9","size":330557,"upload_time":"2026-02-08T14:47:10","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-02-08T14:47:10.111091Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/ed/f1/c92e75a0eb18bb10845e792054ded113010de958b6d4998e201c029417bb/pypdf-6.7.0-py3-none-any.whl","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":false,"digests":{"blake2b_256":"10458340de1c752bfda2da912ea0fa8c9a432f7de3f6315e82f1c0847811dff6","md5":"0ccd8eda2a4104d4b113a967833fc8bd","sha256":"eb95e244d9f434e6cfd157272283339ef586e593be64ee699c620f756d5c3f7e"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"pypdf-6.7.0.tar.gz","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"0ccd8eda2a4104d4b113a967833fc8bd","packagetype":"sdist","python_version":"source","requires_python":">=3.9","size":5299947,"upload_time":"2026-02-08T14:47:11","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-02-08T14:47:11.897335Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/10/45/8340de1c752bfda2da912ea0fa8c9a432f7de3f6315e82f1c0847811dff6/pypdf-6.7.0.tar.gz","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null}],"vulnerabilities":[{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27026","PYSEC-2026-3015"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires a malformed `/FlateDecode` stream, where the byte-by-byte decompression is used.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3644](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3644).","fixed_in":["6.7.1"],"id":"GHSA-9mvc-8737-8j8h","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-9mvc-8737-8j8h","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27024","PYSEC-2026-3013"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires accessing the children of a `TreeObject`, for example as part of outlines.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3645](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3645).","fixed_in":["6.7.1"],"id":"GHSA-996q-pr4m-cvgq","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-996q-pr4m-cvgq","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27025","PYSEC-2026-3024"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires parsing the `/ToUnicode` entry of a font with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3646](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3646).","fixed_in":["6.7.1"],"id":"GHSA-wgvp-vg3v-2xq3","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-wgvp-vg3v-2xq3","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27628","PYSEC-2026-3005"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires reading the file.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.2).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf users cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3655](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3655).","fixed_in":["6.7.2"],"id":"GHSA-2rw7-x74f-jg35","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-2rw7-x74f-jg35","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27888","PYSEC-2026-3027"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to the RAM being exhausted. This requires accessing the `xfa` property of a reader or writer and the corresponding stream being compressed using `/FlateDecode`.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.3](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.3).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf projects cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3658](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3658).","fixed_in":["6.7.3"],"id":"GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-28351","PYSEC-2026-3017"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing the content stream using the RunLengthDecode filter.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.4](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.4).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3664](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3664).","fixed_in":["6.7.4"],"id":"GHSA-f2v5-7jq9-h8cg","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-f2v5-7jq9-h8cg","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-28804","PYSEC-2026-3014"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires accessing a stream which uses the `/ASCIIHexDecode` filter.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.5](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.5).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3666](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3666).","fixed_in":["6.7.5"],"id":"GHSA-9m86-7pmv-2852","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-9m86-7pmv-2852","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-31826","PYSEC-2026-3019"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing a content stream with a rather large `/Length` value, regardless of the actual data length inside the stream.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.8.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.8.0).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3675](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3675).\n\nAs far as we are aware, this mostly affects reading from buffers of unknown size, as returned by `open(\"file.pdf\", mode=\"rb\")` for example. Passing a file path or a `BytesIO` buffer to *pypdf* instead does not seem to trigger the vulnerability.","fixed_in":["6.8.0"],"id":"GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-33123","PYSEC-2026-3023"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and/or large memory usage. This requires accessing an array-based stream with lots of entries.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.9.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.9.1).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3686](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3686).","fixed_in":["6.9.1"],"id":"GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-33699","PYSEC-2026-3012"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires reading a file in non-strict mode.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.9.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.9.2).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf users cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3693](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3693).","fixed_in":["6.9.2"],"id":"GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-40260","PYSEC-2026-3006"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing the XMP metadata.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.0).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3724](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3724).","fixed_in":["6.10.0"],"id":"GHSA-3crg-w4f6-42mx","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-3crg-w4f6-42mx","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-41168","PYSEC-2026-3021"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires cross-reference streams with wrong large `/Size` values or object streams with wrong large `/N` values.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3733](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3733).","fixed_in":["6.10.1"],"id":"GHSA-jj6c-8h6c-hppx","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-jj6c-8h6c-hppx","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-41313","PYSEC-2026-3007"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires loading a PDF with a large trailer `/Size` value in incremental mode.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3735](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3735).","fixed_in":["6.10.2"],"id":"GHSA-4pxv-j86v-mhcw","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-4pxv-j86v-mhcw","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-41312","PYSEC-2026-3011"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to the RAM being exhausted. This requires accessing a stream compressed using `/FlateDecode` with a `/Predictor` unequal 1 and large predictor parameters.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3734](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3734).","fixed_in":["6.10.2"],"id":"GHSA-7gw9-cf7v-778f","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-7gw9-cf7v-778f","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-41314","PYSEC-2026-3026"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to the RAM being exhausted. This requires accessing an image using `/FlateDecode` with large size values.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3734](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3734).","fixed_in":["6.10.2"],"id":"GHSA-x284-j5p8-9c5p","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-x284-j5p8-9c5p","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-48156","PYSEC-2026-3004"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires cross-reference streams with `/W [0 0 0]` values and large `/Size` values.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf developers are unable to upgrade their apps immediately, they should consider applying the changes from PR [#3791](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3791).","fixed_in":["6.12.0"],"id":"GHSA-248m-82v9-q6g6","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-248m-82v9-q6g6","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-48155","PYSEC-2026-3016"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires extracting text in layout mode with large character offsets.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf developers are unable to immediately upgrade, they should consider applying the changes from PR [#3790](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3790).","fixed_in":["6.12.0"],"id":"GHSA-cj93-chg6-vgv8","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-cj93-chg6-vgv8","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-49461","PYSEC-2026-3020"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires extracting the text of a page which contains a form XObject with self-references.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3805](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3805).","fixed_in":["6.12.2"],"id":"GHSA-j543-4vmf-qm7v","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-j543-4vmf-qm7v","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-48735","PYSEC-2026-3025"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing large XMP metadata, possibly with lots of unnecessary elements.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.1).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3796](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3796).","fixed_in":["6.12.1"],"id":"GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-49460","PYSEC-2026-3010"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires accessing a stream which uses the `/FlateDecode` filter with a PNG predictor.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3806](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3806).","fixed_in":["6.12.2"],"id":"GHSA-5hgr-hg42-57jg","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-5hgr-hg42-57jg","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-54531","PYSEC-2026-3022"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires merging a file with outlines into a writer.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.13.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.13.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3830](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3830).","fixed_in":["6.13.0"],"id":"GHSA-m2v9-299j-rv96","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-m2v9-299j-rv96","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-54530","PYSEC-2026-3009"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires extracting the text in layout mode.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.13.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.13.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3830](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3830).","fixed_in":["6.13.0"],"id":"GHSA-52x6-gq3r-vpf4","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-52x6-gq3r-vpf4","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-57204"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage, as `MAX_DECLARED_STREAM_LENGTH` is sometimes ignored. This requires parsing a content stream without a `/Length` value.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.13.3](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.13.3).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3871](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3871).","fixed_in":["6.13.3"],"id":"GHSA-jm82-fx9c-mx94","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-jm82-fx9c-mx94","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-54651","PYSEC-2026-3018"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires merging a file with threads/articles into a writer.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.13.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.13.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf users cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3839](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3839).","fixed_in":["6.13.1"],"id":"GHSA-g9xf-7f8q-9mcj","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-g9xf-7f8q-9mcj","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-33123","GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and/or large memory usage. This requires accessing an array-based stream with lots of entries.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.9.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.9.1).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3686](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3686).","fixed_in":["6.9.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3023","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3023","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-54531","GHSA-m2v9-299j-rv96"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires merging a file with outlines into a writer.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.13.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.13.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3830](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3830).","fixed_in":["6.13.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3022","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3022","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-28351","GHSA-f2v5-7jq9-h8cg"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing the content stream using the RunLengthDecode filter.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.4](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.4).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3664](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3664).","fixed_in":["6.7.4"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3017","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3017","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-31826","GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing a content stream with a rather large `/Length` value, regardless of the actual data length inside the stream.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.8.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.8.0).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3675](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3675).\n\nAs far as we are aware, this mostly affects reading from buffers of unknown size, as returned by `open(\"file.pdf\", mode=\"rb\")` for example. Passing a file path or a `BytesIO` buffer to *pypdf* instead does not seem to trigger the vulnerability.","fixed_in":["6.8.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3019","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3019","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-49461","GHSA-j543-4vmf-qm7v"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires extracting the text of a page which contains a form XObject with self-references.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3805](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3805).","fixed_in":["6.12.2"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3020","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3020","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-54651","GHSA-g9xf-7f8q-9mcj"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires merging a file with threads/articles into a writer.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.13.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.13.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf users cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3839](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3839).","fixed_in":["6.13.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3018","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3018","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-41168","GHSA-jj6c-8h6c-hppx"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires cross-reference streams with wrong large `/Size` values or object streams with wrong large `/N` values.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3733](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3733).","fixed_in":["6.10.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3021","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3021","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-41312","GHSA-7gw9-cf7v-778f"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to the RAM being exhausted. This requires accessing a stream compressed using `/FlateDecode` with a `/Predictor` unequal 1 and large predictor parameters.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3734](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3734).","fixed_in":["6.10.2"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3011","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3011","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-41313","GHSA-4pxv-j86v-mhcw"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires loading a PDF with a large trailer `/Size` value in incremental mode.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3735](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3735).","fixed_in":["6.10.2"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3007","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3007","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-48156","GHSA-248m-82v9-q6g6"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires cross-reference streams with `/W [0 0 0]` values and large `/Size` values.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf developers are unable to upgrade their apps immediately, they should consider applying the changes from PR [#3791](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3791).","fixed_in":["6.12.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3004","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3004","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27628","GHSA-2rw7-x74f-jg35"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires reading the file.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.2).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf users cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3655](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3655).","fixed_in":["6.7.2"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3005","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3005","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-40260","GHSA-3crg-w4f6-42mx"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing the XMP metadata.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.0).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3724](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3724).","fixed_in":["6.10.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3006","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3006","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-28804","GHSA-9m86-7pmv-2852"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires accessing a stream which uses the `/ASCIIHexDecode` filter.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.5](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.5).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3666](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3666).","fixed_in":["6.7.5"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3014","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3014","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27025","GHSA-wgvp-vg3v-2xq3"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires parsing the `/ToUnicode` entry of a font with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3646](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3646).","fixed_in":["6.7.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3024","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3024","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-41314","GHSA-x284-j5p8-9c5p"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to the RAM being exhausted. This requires accessing an image using `/FlateDecode` with large size values.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.10.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.10.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3734](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3734).","fixed_in":["6.10.2"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3026","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3026","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-48155","GHSA-cj93-chg6-vgv8"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires extracting text in layout mode with large character offsets.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf developers are unable to immediately upgrade, they should consider applying the changes from PR [#3790](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3790).","fixed_in":["6.12.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3016","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3016","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-49460","GHSA-5hgr-hg42-57jg"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires accessing a stream which uses the `/FlateDecode` filter with a PNG predictor.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.2).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3806](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3806).","fixed_in":["6.12.2"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3010","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3010","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27026","GHSA-9mvc-8737-8j8h"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires a malformed `/FlateDecode` stream, where the byte-by-byte decompression is used.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3644](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3644).","fixed_in":["6.7.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3015","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3015","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27024","GHSA-996q-pr4m-cvgq"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires accessing the children of a `TreeObject`, for example as part of outlines.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3645](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3645).","fixed_in":["6.7.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3013","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3013","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-54530","GHSA-52x6-gq3r-vpf4"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires extracting the text in layout mode.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.13.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.13.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3830](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3830).","fixed_in":["6.13.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3009","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3009","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-48735","GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing large XMP metadata, possibly with lots of unnecessary elements.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.1).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3796](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3796).","fixed_in":["6.12.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3025","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3025","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-33699","GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires reading a file in non-strict mode.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.9.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.9.2).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf users cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3693](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3693).","fixed_in":["6.9.2"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3012","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3012","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-27888","GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to the RAM being exhausted. This requires accessing the `xfa` property of a reader or writer and the corresponding stream being compressed using `/FlateDecode`.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.3](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.3).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf projects cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3658](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3658).","fixed_in":["6.7.3"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3027","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3027","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-59938","PYSEC-2026-3611"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires loading images where the declared size values are much too large compared to the actual data.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.14.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.14.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3888](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3888).","fixed_in":["6.14.0"],"id":"GHSA-5qjq-93h5-hrgp","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-5qjq-93h5-hrgp","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-59937","PYSEC-2026-3610"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires cross-reference streams with repeated malformed cross-reference streams.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.14.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.14.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3887](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3887).","fixed_in":["6.14.0"],"id":"GHSA-55h5-xmcq-c37v","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-55h5-xmcq-c37v","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-59935","PYSEC-2026-3613"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires parsing the content stream of a page with a not terminated inline image, as done when extracting the page text for example. It only affects the ASCII85 and ASCIIHex filters.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.14.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.14.2).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3892](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3892).","fixed_in":["6.14.2"],"id":"GHSA-g867-7843-wf8q","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-g867-7843-wf8q","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-59936","PYSEC-2026-3612"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires parsing the content stream of a page with a not terminated inline image, as done when extracting the page text for example.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.14.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.14.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3891](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3891).","fixed_in":["6.14.1"],"id":"GHSA-5xf7-4p34-54qr","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-5xf7-4p34-54qr","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-59935","GHSA-g867-7843-wf8q"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires parsing the content stream of a page with a not terminated inline image, as done when extracting the page text for example. It only affects the ASCII85 and ASCIIHex filters.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.14.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.14.2).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3892](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3892).","fixed_in":["6.14.2"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3613","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3613","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-59937","GHSA-55h5-xmcq-c37v"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires cross-reference streams with repeated malformed cross-reference streams.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.14.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.14.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3887](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3887).","fixed_in":["6.14.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3610","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3610","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-59936","GHSA-5xf7-4p34-54qr"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires parsing the content stream of a page with a not terminated inline image, as done when extracting the page text for example.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.14.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.14.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3891](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3891).","fixed_in":["6.14.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3612","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3612","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-59938","GHSA-5qjq-93h5-hrgp"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires loading images where the declared size values are much too large compared to the actual data.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.14.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.14.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3888](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3888).","fixed_in":["6.14.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3611","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3611","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-71852","PYSEC-2026-3656"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires parsing the font width entries of a font with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.15.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.15.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3946](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3946).","fixed_in":["6.15.0"],"id":"GHSA-fwg2-594c-jp42","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-fwg2-594c-jp42","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-71870","PYSEC-2026-3655"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires parsing the `/ToUnicode` entry of a font with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.15.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.15.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3944](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3944).","fixed_in":["6.15.0"],"id":"GHSA-fp3f-mc75-235c","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-fp3f-mc75-235c","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-71870","GHSA-fp3f-mc75-235c"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires parsing the `/ToUnicode` entry of a font with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.15.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.15.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3944](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3944).","fixed_in":["6.15.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3655","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3655","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-71852","GHSA-fwg2-594c-jp42"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires parsing the font width entries of a font with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.15.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.15.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3946](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3946).","fixed_in":["6.15.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3656","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3656","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102993"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires accessing the page labels of a document with large Roman numerals.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.17.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.17.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4047](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4047).","fixed_in":["6.17.0"],"id":"GHSA-qv6h-rv94-w285","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-qv6h-rv94-w285","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-103000"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires accessing the page labels of a document with large alphabetical labels.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.19.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.19.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4096](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4096).","fixed_in":["6.19.0"],"id":"GHSA-w23x-9jrw-r45c","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-w23x-9jrw-r45c","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102995"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires parsing the `/ToUnicode` entry of a font with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.18.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.18.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4071](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4071).","fixed_in":["6.18.1"],"id":"GHSA-fp3h-c4fm-7vvf","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-fp3h-c4fm-7vvf","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102994"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires reading a PDF document with long indirect object headers, not terminated by whitespace.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.18.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.18.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4055](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4055).","fixed_in":["6.18.0"],"id":"GHSA-5jq2-8x83-x246","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-5jq2-8x83-x246","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-84309"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires a (usually writing) code path where `TreeObject.insert_child` is involved.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.16.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.16.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3964](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3964).","fixed_in":["6.16.0"],"id":"GHSA-jp53-mhqp-8xcg","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-jp53-mhqp-8xcg","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-84310"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires accessing the outlines of a document with either lots of entries or nested outlines with long re-used nesting paths.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.16.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.16.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3966](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3966).","fixed_in":["6.16.1"],"id":"GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-84311"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires extracting the text of a page with lots of XForm objects, where some of them might be re-used.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.16.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.16.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3966](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3966).","fixed_in":["6.16.1"],"id":"GHSA-763m-79hh-57f2","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-763m-79hh-57f2","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102998"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires updating form field values with flattening enabled, which triggers appearance stream generation.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.19.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.19.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4087](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4087).","fixed_in":["6.19.0"],"id":"GHSA-php9-fj8v-98fj","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-php9-fj8v-98fj","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102996"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires parsing the `/Widths` entry of a TrueType or Type1 fonts with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.18.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.18.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4072](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4072).","fixed_in":["6.18.1"],"id":"GHSA-g9cg-prrw-2r8q","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-g9cg-prrw-2r8q","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-82398"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires a call to `read_until_whitespace` with an input which does not have whitespace for a long time.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.15.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.15.0).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3947](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3947).","fixed_in":["6.15.0"],"id":"GHSA-fc8x-2rww-xw9m","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-fc8x-2rww-xw9m","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102997"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires a partially malformed `/FlateDecode` stream, where the byte-by-byte decompression is used.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.18.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.18.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4073](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4073).","fixed_in":["6.18.1"],"id":"GHSA-jw7q-gvrg-4vj3","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-jw7q-gvrg-4vj3","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102999"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires accessing the embedded files through the dictionary-based API.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.19.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.19.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4081](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4081).","fixed_in":["6.19.0"],"id":"GHSA-v247-6f48-mgcj","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-v247-6f48-mgcj","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-82398","GHSA-fc8x-2rww-xw9m"],"details":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires a call to `read_until_whitespace` with an input which does not have whitespace for a long time.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.15.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.15.0).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3947](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3947).","fixed_in":["6.15.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3912","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3912","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-84310","GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires accessing the outlines of a document with either lots of entries or nested outlines with long re-used nesting paths.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.16.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.16.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3966](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3966).","fixed_in":["6.16.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3910","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3910","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-84311","GHSA-763m-79hh-57f2"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires extracting the text of a page with lots of XForm objects, where some of them might be re-used.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.16.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.16.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3966](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3966).","fixed_in":["6.16.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3911","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3911","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-84309","GHSA-jp53-mhqp-8xcg"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires a (usually writing) code path where `TreeObject.insert_child` is involved.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.16.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.16.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3964](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3964).","fixed_in":["6.16.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-3913","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-3913","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102994","GHSA-5jq2-8x83-x246"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires reading a PDF document with long indirect object headers, not terminated by whitespace.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.18.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.18.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4055](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4055).","fixed_in":["6.18.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-4153","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-4153","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102995","GHSA-fp3h-c4fm-7vvf"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires parsing the `/ToUnicode` entry of a font with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.18.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.18.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4071](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4071).","fixed_in":["6.18.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-4154","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-4154","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-103000","GHSA-w23x-9jrw-r45c"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires accessing the page labels of a document with large alphabetical labels.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.19.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.19.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4096](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4096).","fixed_in":["6.19.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-4160","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-4160","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102999","GHSA-v247-6f48-mgcj"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires accessing the embedded files through the dictionary-based API.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.19.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.19.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4081](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4081).","fixed_in":["6.19.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-4159","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-4159","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102997","GHSA-jw7q-gvrg-4vj3"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires a partially malformed `/FlateDecode` stream, where the byte-by-byte decompression is used.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.18.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.18.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4073](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4073).","fixed_in":["6.18.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-4156","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-4156","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102996","GHSA-g9cg-prrw-2r8q"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires parsing the `/Widths` entry of a TrueType or Type1 fonts with unusually large values, for example during text extraction.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.18.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.18.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4072](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4072).","fixed_in":["6.18.1"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-4155","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-4155","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102993","GHSA-qv6h-rv94-w285"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires accessing the page labels of a document with large Roman numerals.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.17.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.17.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4047](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4047).","fixed_in":["6.17.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-4158","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-4158","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":["CVE-2026-102998","GHSA-php9-fj8v-98fj"],"details":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires updating form field values with flattening enabled, which triggers appearance stream generation.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.19.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.19.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4087](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4087).","fixed_in":["6.19.0"],"id":"PYSEC-2026-4157","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-4157","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null}]}
